{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":482854,"name":"MB","username":"mblabs.io","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/dec6dc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-04T06:39:12.506Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot desktop 0.39.0 on macOS cannot reach its cloud computer. It shows “Can’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer” and tells IT to allow \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorrm.com\u003c/code\u003e; Retry does not recover.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI followed the support guidance from the matching macOS 0.39.0 report: I saved an explicit Privacy Mode choice in the Cursor dashboard, kept data sharing off, quit Grok Bot with Cmd+Q, reopened it, and clicked Retry once. The failure remains.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Grok Bot 0.39.0 on macOS.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe app shows “Can’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer” and Retry fails.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Cursor dashboard Settings, save Privacy Mode with data sharing off.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot (Cmd+Q), reopen it, and click Retry once.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe app still cannot connect to the computer.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter Privacy Mode is saved, Grok Bot should connect to its cloud computer and load normally. The app should not continue showing the firewall/VPN message or a non-working Retry action.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot desktop 0.39.0\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: macOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot (not Cursor IDE)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003en/a — Grok Bot never connects, so no Request ID is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-additional-information-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-additional-information-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNetwork evidence: \u003ccode\u003ecursorrm.com\u003c/code\u003e returns DNS NXDOMAIN through the local resolver and independently through Cloudflare 1.1.1.1 and Google 8.8.8.8. No macOS system proxy is configured. Because the registrable domain does not resolve publicly, a firewall allow-list cannot make \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorrm.com\u003c/code\u003e reachable. Please check the account’s Grok Bot computer provisioning and the endpoint/configuration behind this message.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482854-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482854-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-04T11:40:12.964Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":18,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":91.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170536,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-macos-cant-reach-computer","display_username":"MB","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":5,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136084,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-39-0-macos-cant-reach-computer/170536/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":482897,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-04T07:32:06.119Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and the network checks. A couple quick points will save time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe domain in that message is \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e with v-m, not \u003ccode\u003ecursorrm.com\u003c/code\u003e, so your DNS checks were against a name we don’t use. Bare \u003ccode\u003ecursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e also should not resolve on its own. Only per-region hosts work. Also, your Privacy Mode was already saved correctly even before you changed it, so that step isn’t related here. That recommendation was for a different case.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn our side, your Grok Bot computer is healthy, and Grok Bot on your phone is using it fine. It ran a task this morning at about 09:19 Cairo time. But Grok Bot on your Mac has not reached our servers at all since Aug 28. That means the issue is somewhere between that Mac and the internet, not the computer itself.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the Mac, please try this and tell me what you see:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen Grok Bot → Settings and confirm you’re signed in as \u003ccode\u003emblabs.io@gmail.com\u003c/code\u003e using the same account as on your phone. If it’s a different account, sign out and sign in with that one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen System Settings → Network → Firewall. If it’s on, click Options and make sure Grok Bot is allowed. Also check any security or filtering tools like Little Snitch, LuLu, antivirus, parental controls, or a DNS filter, and allow Grok Bot there too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen Terminal, run these four commands, and copy the full output:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003enslookup api2.cursor.sh\nnslookup test.us8.cursorvm.com\ncurl -sI https://api2.cursor.sh | head -1\ncurl -sI https://test.us8.cursorvm.com | head -1\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAny HTTP line in the last two is fine, even 404. We only care whether they connect.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFully quit Grok Bot with \u003ccode\u003eCmd+Q\u003c/code\u003e, reopen it, and wait about 2 minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the message is still there, connect the Mac to your phone hotspot, then quit and reopen Grok Bot again, and wait 2 minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReply with the Terminal output, whether the hotspot test connected, the attempt time with timezone, and the Grok Bot version from Settings. This will clearly show where it’s getting stuck.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-04T07:32:06.119Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":11.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170536,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-macos-cant-reach-computer","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-39-0-macos-cant-reach-computer/170536/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":483175,"name":"MB","username":"mblabs.io","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/dec6dc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-04T11:41:00.716Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eYou’re right — the \u003ccode\u003e*.cursorrm.com\u003c/code\u003e hostname in the first post was my mistake.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eValidated today (Africa/Cairo):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe desktop app is signed in with the same account as the phone.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003emacOS firewall is disabled and no system proxy is configured.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eapi2.cursor.sh\u003c/code\u003e resolves and \u003ccode\u003ecurl -sI https://api2.cursor.sh | head -1\u003c/code\u003e returns \u003ccode\u003eHTTP/2 200\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003etest.us8.cursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e resolves and \u003ccode\u003ecurl -sI https://test.us8.cursorvm.com | head -1\u003c/code\u003e returns \u003ccode\u003eHTTP/1.1 404 Not Found\u003c/code\u003e, so it connects as expected. Bare \u003ccode\u003ecursorvm.com\u003c/code\u003e has no A record.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAfter fully quitting Grok Bot, reopening it, and waiting about two minutes, the failure remains.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI repeated that exact test on a phone hotspot; the result was the same.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDuring in-app \u003ccode\u003eRetrying…\u003c/code\u003e, I observed no established Grok Bot TCP connection.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot version: \u003ccode\u003e0.39.0\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat log, diagnostic, or next macOS check would you like me to collect to determine why the desktop client is not initiating a connection?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-04T14:51:20.306Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":1.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170536,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-macos-cant-reach-computer","display_username":"MB","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136084,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-39-0-macos-cant-reach-computer/170536/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[482854,482897,483175]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"},{"id":308,"name":"privacy-mode","slug":"privacy-mode"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot 0.39.0 macOS — can\u0026rsquo;t reach computer","id":170536,"title":"Grok Bot 0.39.0 macOS — can't reach computer","posts_count":3,"created_at":"2026-09-04T06:39:12.439Z","views":51,"reply_count":1,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-04T11:41:00.716Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-macos-cant-reach-computer","category_id":6,"word_count":842,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":136084,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":null,"slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_170536","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":6,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"